; fas9_assoc_core.scr - facit script of step 9.10 (F9.11 persistent subentities; the observed parts of F9.12): the associative
; framework's network, actions, dependencies, parameters and bodies of the associative surfaces, and the persistent
; subentity managers of surfaces and solids. Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_assoc_core.scr
; It starts from AutoCAD's own acad.dwt (a new empty drawing) and uses plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (the core has
; none). SURFACEASSOCIATIVITY 1 makes every surface remember how it was made (an ACDBASSOCNETWORK with one action per
; surface, its dependencies on the profile and path curves, its parameters and its action body); DELOBJ 0 keeps the
; profiles, so two actions can share one (a line extruded twice: two actions, one geometry).
;
; Files (acad_<version>_dxf_<theme>[_<change>][_bin].dxf, 2000 … 2018; the core cannot save R13/R14):
;   assoc_core                       the drawing as drawn: a line extruded twice (two actions, one geometry), a closed polyline
;                                    extruded as a surface, a revolve, a sweep, a loft, a plane surface
;   assoc_core surface_erased        the second extrusion of the shared line erased (its action, parameters, dependencies and body
;                                    go; the line and the first extrusion's action stay: B19 by AutoCAD itself)
;   assoc_core profile_erased        the shared line erased
;   assoc_core profile_moved         the shared line moved (the actions' geometry changes)
;   assoc_solids                     the persistent subentity manager of solids: two boxes and a cylinder
;   assoc_solids union               the two boxes united
;
; What AutoCAD 2025's core cannot do, and what is therefore "ej testat" (plan 2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md, F9.11, F9.12):
;   - ACDBASSOCALIGNEDDIMACTIONBODY and ACDBASSOCOSNAPPOINTREFACTIONPARAM: the core's dimension with endpoint snaps makes a
;     DIMASSOC (step 9.17), not an action body; the only AutoCAD files with the two are the Autodesk example drawing saved in
;     2007 … 2018 (build/test-data/libre/example_*.dxf)
;   - the persistent subentity manager's history entries (fillet, chamfer or Boolean history of a solid, a surface made from the
;     edges of another): FILLETEDGE, CHAMFEREDGE and SOLIDEDIT pick faces and edges on the screen, which the core has not; the
;     corpus' managers with entries (Surface_2004, example_*, acad_*_surfaces.dxf, acad_2013_dxf_solids.dxf) are read as records
;     that stay as they were
;   - an edge, face or vertex "added" to or "removed" from a manager by an edit of a solid: the same
; The plain surface and solid commands below do work.
_.SURFACEASSOCIATIVITY
1
_.SURFACEMODELINGMODE
0
_.DELOBJ
0
_.ISOLINES
8
_.ZOOM
_Window
-20,-20
320,100
; A line extruded twice along a direction (its footprint is then larger than the line: a window selects the line alone)
_.LINE
0,0,0
10,0,0

_.EXTRUDE
_L

_Direction
0,0,0
80,0,30
_.EXTRUDE
_P

_Direction
0,0,0
120,0,40
; A closed polyline extruded as a surface (a taper)
_.PLINE
0,60
20,60
20,80
0,80
_Close
_.EXTRUDE
_MOde
_SUrface
_L

_Taper
5
15
; A revolve of a line
_.LINE
120,0,0
135,10,30

_.REVOLVE
_L

_Z
300
; A sweep of a line along a 3D polyline
_.LINE
160,0,0
170,0,0

_.3DPOLY
165,0,0
180,20,20
190,40,30

_.SWEEP
_Window
158,-1
172,1

_L
; A loft of three circles
_.CIRCLE
180,70,0
12
_.CIRCLE
185,70,20
8
_.CIRCLE
180,75,40
15
_.LOFT
_MOde
_SUrface
_Window
160,55
200,95


; A plane surface from a closed polyline
_.PLINE
260,0
300,0
300,30
260,30
_Close
_.PLANESURF
_Object
_L

;EXPECT ACDBASSOCNETWORK ACDBASSOCACTION ACDBASSOCDEPENDENCY ACDBASSOCEDGEACTIONPARAM ACDBASSOCEXTRUDEDSURFACEACTIONBODY
;SAVE assoc_core
; Each change is made after an UNDO mark and taken back to it (a plain U would undo the SAVEAS)
_.UNDO
_Mark
; The second extrusion of the shared line erased: the window takes both surfaces and the line, the removal leaves the second
_.ERASE
_Window
-1,-1
135,5
_Remove
_Window
-1,-1
125,5

;SAVE assoc_core surface_erased
_.UNDO
_Back
_.UNDO
_Mark
; The shared line erased (a window around it: its own footprint is the only one that small)
_.ERASE
_Window
-1,-1
11,1

;SAVE assoc_core profile_erased
_.UNDO
_Back
_.UNDO
_Mark
; The shared line moved
_.MOVE
_Window
-1,-1
11,1

0,0
0,5
;SAVE assoc_core profile_moved
_.UNDO
_Back
; Solids: two boxes and a cylinder (the manager of a drawing with solids), then the boxes united
_.SOLIDHIST
1
_.BOX
300,100,0
310,120,30
_.BOX
305,105,5
315,125,35
_.CYLINDER
330,110,0
4
50
;SAVE assoc_solids
_.UNION
_Window
299,99
316,126

;SAVE assoc_solids union
